# Data files
data/raw/**/*.csv
data/raw/**/*.xlsx
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# Compressed DB snapshots now live in R2 (state/*.db.gz); never commit them.
data/bddk_data.db.gz
data/bank_audit.db.gz

# External reports — third-party PDFs, do not redistribute
data/external_reports/

# EVDS HTTP response cache (rebuilt on demand)
data/evds_cache/

# BIST (Yahoo) HTTP response cache (rebuilt on demand)
data/bist_cache/

# Per-bank audit-report PDFs — 2 GB+ of bank-published PDFs.
# Kept local only; structured rows live in bddk_data.db (bank_audit_* tables).
# URL config IS committed (data/banks/audit_report_urls.json) so the pipeline
# is reproducible from scratch.
data/audit_reports/

# Auto-generated catalogue (regenerated by a scraper probe)
scripts/_weekly_catalogue.json

# Audit repair-campaign byproducts (scratch / regenerable; see docs/AUDIT_PIPELINE.md)
# NB: data/metric_knowledge/ is NOT scratch — it's the committed banking-metric
# knowledge registry (hand-curated reference data; see docs/BANKING_METRICS.md).
data/eye/
data/fleet_scratch.db
data/_anomalies_*.txt
data/run_*.cmd

# scratch_bench_unit_detection.py byproducts — the PDFs it pulls from R2 and the
# per-filing result it writes. Both are regenerable from a workflow dispatch.
data/_bench/
bench_unit_detection.json

# Economy chart-reproduction diagnostics — source-report PDFs + page-image crops
# pulled while building the /economy pages, consolidated under data/albaraka_reports/
# ({bop,budget,growth,inflation,trade}/). Local-only; the dashboard data lives in
# D1 (evds_series etc.), not these. Kept on disk, out of git.
data/albaraka_*/

# Reports
reports/**/*.pdf
reports/**/*.html
reports/**/*.xlsx

# Logs
logs/**/*.log
data/_*.log
data/_tmp_*.pdf

# Environment variables
.env
.env.local

# System files
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp
temp/
tmp/

# Chrome driver
chromedriver
chromedriver.exe

# Backup files
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.backup
bddk_data.db.bak*

# Keep directory structure but ignore contents
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep
!reports/.gitkeep
!logs/.gitkeep

# Agent / scratch work (not versioned)
_scratch/

# Claude Code local state — per-user, never committed
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/worktrees/

# Next.js / Cloudflare / OpenNext local build artefacts (not versioned)
node_modules/
.next/
.wrangler/
.open-next/
.dev.vars
# Migration log from one-shot migrate_pdfs_to_r2.py runs
migrate.log


# Local pipeline run logs
data/*.log

# Design archive — mockups, screenshots and the artefact register are kept
# LOCAL ONLY. They are superseded iterations (five generations of the
# regulation tab alone) that cost ~16MB in the repo and serve no reader of
# the public code. web/DESIGN.md is the design *law* and stays versioned;
# this is the *archive*. Keep the files on disk — they are still the record
# of why a page looks the way it does.
docs/design/

# Internal business/strategy assessments — LOCAL ONLY. These evaluate the
# product and the business (positioning, moat, weaknesses, site ratings)
# rather than the data pipeline. The extraction and validator post-mortems
# in docs/knowledge/ stay public: those demonstrate the rigour behind the
# numbers, which is worth publishing. These do not.
docs/knowledge/strategic-review-2026-07.md
docs/knowledge/website-evaluation-2026-07-12.md
docs/knowledge/dashboard-audit.md
docs/knowledge/2026-07-13-sector-pages-consistency-audit.md
docs/knowledge/website-evaluation-2026-07-25.md

# Reading lists — LOCAL ONLY. These index *other people's* work (broker
# earnings previews, rating actions, multilateral reports, FT chart references,
# BBVA outlook editions) rather than documenting our own pipeline. Kept on disk
# as reference; nothing downstream reads them, the deep links age out within a
# quarter, and a reader of the public code does not need our reading list. The
# extraction and validator post-mortems in docs/knowledge/ stay public — those
# are about our numbers.
# Generated triage output (scripts/triage_partitions.py, watch_cross_period.py).
# Regenerated on every run and republished as a workflow artifact, so committing
# it would churn git with a dated copy of a report nothing downstream reads. The
# FINDINGS live in a dated write-up alongside the other post-mortems.
docs/knowledge/triage/

docs/knowledge/external-reports/
docs/knowledge/bbva-economic-outlook/
docs/knowledge/ft-visual-journalism/
